Line A makes $\frac{1}{4}$ of the output, line B makes $\frac{1}{3}$, and line C makes the remainder, which is $1 - \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{3} = \frac{5}{12}$.

The chance of shipping a sound item is $1$ from line A and $\frac{9}{10}$ from each of lines B and C.

P(\text{sound}) = \frac{1}{4} \cdot 1 + \frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{9}{10} + \frac{5}{12} \cdot \frac{9}{10} = \frac{1}{4} + \frac{3}{10} + \frac{3}{8} = \frac{37}{40}

Line C's contribution is $\frac{5}{12} \cdot \frac{9}{10} = \frac{3}{8}$, so

P(C \mid \text{sound}) = \frac{3/8}{37/40} = \frac{15}{37}
